Let $[a,b]\subset\mathbb{R}$ be a closed bounded interval, and let $f,g,h:[a,b]\to(0,\infty)$ be positive continuous functions satisfying:
\begin{itemize}
\item $f(x)\le h(x)$ for every $x\in[a,b]$;
\item the quotient $x\mapsto f(x)/h(x)$ is (monotonically) decreasing on $[a,b]$;
\item both $f$ and $g$ are (monotonically) increasing on $[a,b]$.
\end{itemize}
Let $\varphi:[0,\infty)\to[0,\infty)$ be a convex function with $\varphi(0)=0$.

Determine all pairs of real exponents $(\delta,\lambda)$ for which the inequality
\[
\frac{\int_a^b f(x)\,dx}{\int_a^b h(x)\,dx} \;\ge\; \frac{\left(\int_a^b \varphi(f(x))\,g(x)\,dx\right)^{\delta}}{\left(\int_a^b \varphi(h(x))\,g(x)\,dx\right)^{\lambda}}
\]
holds for every choice of $f$, $g$, $h$, and $\varphi$ satisfying the above hypotheses.

